IMPORT prelude

-- Early Childhood Development Centres Act 2017 (Singapore) -- what counts as a regulated pre-school or childcare centre (s 2, s 3 and
-- the Schedule), the offence of operating without a licence (s 6), when a licence lapses (s 15), the cap on financial penalties
-- (s 16(2)(g)), who can be directed to wind a closing centre down (s 18(3)), disqualified key appointment holders (s 19), older
-- children at a centre (s 20(2)), the maximum penalties and composition sums (ss 6, 17, 18, 19, 35, 38, 39, 45 and 42), and which
-- decisions can be appealed to the Minister (s 43).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation --
-- "version in force from 1/7/2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ECDCA2017.txt. The latest amendment annotated in
-- the text is Act 14 of 2025 w.e.f. 1 July 2026 (Schedule item 5, homes licensed under the Social Residential Homes Act 2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it decides which childcare centres and kindergartens must be licensed, and
-- what happens to parents and children when a centre closes. SCOPED to the provisions a parent, an operator or a centre's manager
-- most often meets. Not encoded: the application, renewal and transfer procedure (ss 7, 8, 13) beyond appeal rights; security
-- deposits (s 12); modification of conditions (s 11); the approval regimes for staff and third-party educators (Parts 3 and 4)
-- beyond appeal rights; codes of practice (s 36); powers of entry (s 37); corporate liability (ss 40, 41); secrecy (s 45) beyond
-- its penalty; service of documents (s 47); and everything left to regulations (s 51), none of which was retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Early Childhood Development Centres Act 2017 -- centres`

§§ `2 -- early childhood development service`

-- s 2: "early childhood development service" means "the provision of care or education, or care and education, habitually of 5 or
-- more children who are below 7 years of age, for a fee, reward or profit by a person who is not a relative or guardian of all the
-- children". An "early childhood development centre" is "any premises where any early childhood development service is provided".
GIVEN `children below 7` IS A NUMBER, `habitually` IS A BOOLEAN, `for a fee, reward or profit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the provider is a relative or guardian of all the children` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an early childhood development service` IF
        `children below 7` AT LEAST 5
    AND `habitually`
    AND `for a fee, reward or profit`
    AND (NOT `the provider is a relative or guardian of all the children`)

§§ `3 and the Schedule -- centres the Act does not apply to`

-- s 3(a): the Act does not apply to a centre "(i) operated by or on behalf of the Government; or (ii) specified in the Schedule".
-- Schedule: 1 an enrichment centre which "solely" provides arts or sporting instruction, recreation, or tuition; 2 a centre which
-- "solely provides therapy or other related services for children with special needs"; 3 a playgroup centre (below); 4 a Private
-- Education Act institution with a foreign or international curriculum "covering both pre-primary and full-time primary levels";
-- 5 a home licensed under the Social Residential Homes Act 2025 [Act 14 of 2025 wef 01/07/2026]; 6, 7 places of temporary care and
-- protection and places of safety under the Children and Young Persons Act 1993; 8 a place of safety under the Women's Charter 1961;
-- 9 premises used for a care arrangement under a voluntary care agreement or a fit-person committal order under the CYPA.
DECLARE Centre IS ONE OF
    `a commercial childcare centre`
    `a kindergarten run by a church`
    `an enrichment centre teaching only music and swimming`
    `an enrichment centre that also offers childcare`
    `a special-needs therapy centre`
    `an international school with pre-primary and primary`
    `an international school with pre-primary only`
    `a licensed children's home`
    `a place of safety under the Women's Charter`
    `a Government-operated centre`

GIVEN `the centre` IS A Centre
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the centre` IF
    CONSIDER `the centre`
    WHEN `an enrichment centre teaching only music and swimming` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a special-needs therapy centre` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an international school with pre-primary and primary` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a licensed children's home` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a place of safety under the Women's Charter` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Government-operated centre` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Schedule item 3: "Any playgroup centre the sole purpose of which is the care or education of children who are younger than 4 years
-- of age for a period of 2 hours or shorter each time, through play and activities encouraging socialisation".
GIVEN `all the children are younger than 4` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours each session` IS A NUMBER, `play and socialisation is the sole purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the playgroup is excluded` IF
    `all the children are younger than 4` AND `hours each session` AT MOST 2 AND `play and socialisation is the sole purpose`

§§ `6 -- no operation without a licence`

-- s 6(1): a person must not operate a centre unless the person "(a) is authorised to do so by a licence ...; (b) is exempt ...; or
-- (c) is directed by the Chief Licensing Officer under section 18 to do so despite the expiry or revocation of the licence".
-- (3): fine up to $10,000 or imprisonment up to 12 months or both, "and (b) in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
GIVEN `operates the centre` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `is exempt` IS A BOOLEAN, `is directed under s 18 to carry on` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `operating is an offence` IF
    `operates the centre` AND (NOT `holds a licence`) AND (NOT `is exempt`) AND (NOT `is directed under s 18 to carry on`)

GIVEN `days the offence continues after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlicensed operation` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days the offence continues after conviction`

§§ `15 -- lapse of licence`

-- s 15(1): unless expired or revoked, a licence lapses "(a) if the licensee is an individual, on the date of death of the licensee;
-- (b) if the licensee is a partnership, body corporate or an unincorporated association, on the date the licensee ceases to exist;
-- (c) on the date that the licensee is no longer the owner or a lessee of, or no longer has a licence to occupy, the premises ...; or
-- (d) if no children are enrolled in that centre for a continuous period prescribed". (2): no part of the fee is refunded.
DECLARE Event IS ONE OF
    `the individual licensee dies`
    `the licensee company ceases to exist`
    `the lease of the premises ends`
    `no child is enrolled for the prescribed period`
    `the principal resigns`
    `the licensee is convicted of an offence under the Act`

GIVEN `the event` IS A Event
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence lapses` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `the principal resigns` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the licensee is convicted of an offence under the Act` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `16(2)(g) -- financial penalty`

-- s 16(2)(g): in lieu of revocation, a direction to pay "a financial penalty of such amount as the Chief Licensing Officer thinks fit,
-- being (i) not more than $5,000 for each contravention or non-compliance mentioned in subsection (1) that is the subject; or (ii) in
-- any other case, not more than $5,000". (Read here as $5,000 times the number of contraventions, and $5,000 where none is counted.)
GIVEN `contraventions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum financial penalty` MEANS
    IF `contraventions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 5000 TIMES `contraventions` ELSE 5000

§§ `18(3) -- directions to wind down a closing centre`

-- s 18(2): the purpose is "the orderly cessation ... with minimal disruption to the children". (3): directions may be given to
-- "(a) the licensee; (b) a key appointment holder of the licensee; (c) if there is no key appointment holder of the licensee who is
-- able to comply with the directions, any person who was a key appointment holder of the licensee in the period of 6 months
-- immediately preceding the date of the relevant event". (4)(d): a direction may require the licensee to "refund to the parents or
-- guardian any deposit or fee due to them". (6): failure without reasonable excuse -- $10,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `the licensee`
    `a current key appointment holder`
    `a former key appointment holder`
    `a teacher`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `months before the event that the person left` IS A NUMBER, `a current key appointment holder can comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be directed` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `the licensee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a current key appointment holder` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a former key appointment holder` THEN (NOT `a current key appointment holder can comply`) AND `months before the event that the person left` AT MOST 6
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `19 -- disqualified key appointment holders`

-- s 19(1): a person must not, "without the written consent of the Chief Licensing Officer", act as a key appointment holder if
-- (a) convicted of an offence under this Act; (b) convicted "whether in Singapore or elsewhere" of an offence involving dishonesty;
-- (c) convicted of a prescribed offence; (d) a director of, or concerned in managing, a centre whose licence was refused or revoked
-- (or a child care centre or kindergarten likewise); (e) a teacher whose registration under the Education Act 1957 was cancelled;
-- (f) prohibited under the repealed Act from being employed at a child care centre; (g) refused approval to be deployed, or had it
-- cancelled "(except where the cancellation is due to the centre ceasing to exist)"; (h) not satisfying prescribed criteria.
-- (3): $5,000 or 6 months or both; (4) the same for a licensee who "knowingly allows" it.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `convicted of an offence under this Act`
    `convicted overseas of a dishonesty offence`
    `director of a centre whose licence was revoked`
    `teacher whose registration was cancelled`
    `refused approval to be deployed`
    `approval cancelled because the centre closed`
    `no ground`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is disqualified` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `approval cancelled because the centre closed` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no ground` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `has written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `acting as a key appointment holder is an offence` IF
    `the person is disqualified` `the ground` AND (NOT `has written consent`)

§§ `20(2) -- older children`

-- s 20(1): during operating hours the centre must not be used "for any purpose other than for the ordinary conduct and business of
-- an early childhood development centre". (2): the Chief Licensing Officer may permit the licensee "to receive children who are 7
-- years of age or older but below 14 years of age". INFERENCE: a child of 14 or older is outside both, so is treated as not receivable.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `permitted under s 20(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the centre may receive the child` IF
        `age` LESS THAN 7
    OR  (`age` LESS THAN 14 AND `permitted under s 20(2)`)

§§ `6, 17, 18, 19, 35, 38, 39, 45 and 42 -- penalties and composition`

-- Maximum fines and imprisonment: s 6(3) unlicensed operation $10,000 / 12 months; s 17(7) failing to comply with a safety direction
-- $10,000 / 12 months; s 18(6) failing to comply with a wind-down direction $10,000 / 12 months; s 19(3) disqualified key appointment
-- holder $5,000 / 6 months; s 35(3) records and quality information "a fine not exceeding $5,000" (no imprisonment); s 38 obstruction
-- $5,000 / 6 months; s 39 false information $5,000 / 6 months; s 45(3) disclosure by an officer $5,000 / 6 months.
-- s 42(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of ... (a) one half of the amount of
-- the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000". (Which offences are prescribed was not retrieved.)
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `unlicensed operation`
    `ignoring a safety direction`
    `ignoring a wind-down direction`
    `acting while disqualified`
    `a records offence`
    `obstruction`
    `false information`
    `an officer's unlawful disclosure`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed operation` THEN 10000
    WHEN `ignoring a safety direction` THEN 10000
    WHEN `ignoring a wind-down direction` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed operation` THEN 12
    WHEN `ignoring a safety direction` THEN 12
    WHEN `ignoring a wind-down direction` THEN 12
    WHEN `a records offence` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 6

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

§§ `43 -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 43(1): the former holder of a licence revoked under s 16 may appeal; (2) a licensee may appeal against (a) refusal to renew;
-- (b) a licence condition; (c) a modification of a condition; (d) a code of practice provision; (e) refusal to transfer;
-- (f) regulatory action under s 16; (g) a direction under s 17 or 18; (h)-(k) refusals and cancellations of staff and educator
-- approvals; (3) an applicant may appeal against refusal to grant a licence; (4) a person refused consent under s 19 may appeal.
-- Not listed: a requirement to give a security deposit (s 12), or a refusal of permission under s 20(2). (10): "The Minister's
-- decision on an appeal is final." (12): an appeal "does not affect the operation of the decision appealed against".
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusal to grant a licence`
    `revocation of the licence`
    `a safety direction to close the centre`
    `refusal of consent to a key appointment holder`
    `cancellation of a teacher's approval`
    `a security deposit requirement`
    `refusal of permission to take older children`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision may be appealed to the Minister` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a security deposit requirement` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `refusal of permission to take older children` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
